@@section 1
@@title SQ-LOOT Creative Loot split out of Creative Worldgen, 2026-11-17 ([creative_loot.md](../creative_loot.md) 4, LOOT-01 to LOOT-06; [plan_rules_fixes.md](../plan_rules_fixes.md) sections 5 and 5b, TODO `conventions #15`, `#16`)
@@date 2026-11-17
@@reviewed 2026-11-18
@@jars creativeloot creativeworldgen
@@sources development/creativeLoot kubejs/data/creativeloot/kubejs development/creativeWorldgen/src/main/resources/META-INF/mods.toml kubejs/data/creativedelight/kubejs/miners_delight/loot.js kubejs/data/creativedelight/kubejs/rusticdelight/loot.js kubejs/data/creativedelight/kubejs/veggiesdelight/loot.js kubejs/data/creativedelight/kubejs/vintagedelight/loot.js
@@text
@@text Same behavior expected: every row compares with the pre-split state. Baseline (instance, before the split): `kubejs/exported/baseline_loot_split_2026-11-17/` holds the 2026-11-15 `loot_tables/` dump, `loot_runtime_additions.json` and the 2026-11-16 KubeJS server log (`[loot-tuning] 5 rules -> rewrote 184 tables (...)`). Run rows 01 and 05 before any `/reload` (it truncates the KubeJS log). Needs `creativeloot-1.0.0.jar` and `creativeworldgen-1.0.0.jar` of 2026-11-17 or later.
@@table
## SQ-LOOT-01 | boot: loot engine banner once, tuning line equals the pre-split one
@group A
@commands Boot on the installed jars; read startup.log, the KubeJS server log and latest.log
@pass `[creativeloot] core finished` once in startup.log; `[creativeloot] loaded` in latest.log; `global.LOOT ready`; the `[loot-tuning] N rules -> rewrote M tables (...)` line equals the baseline log's line; no `global.LOOT missing`, no `could not read`, no `queued loot rules failed`, no mixin error on LootModifierManagerMixin
@fails Line differs: a rule file did not load from the new pack (`// requires: creativeloot`), or the CD `loot.js` queue never ran (`global.LOOT.rules` vs the CD jar copy). `global.LOOT missing`: the startup script is not in the jar. Mixin error: SRG name `m_5787_`
@reviewed 2026-11-21
shell test "$(grep -c '\[creativeloot\] core finished' logs/kubejs/startup.log)" = 1
bootexpect \[creativeloot\] loaded
bootreject LootModifierManagerMixin.*(InvalidInjectionException|could not find|failed)
kjsexpect global\.LOOT ready
kjsreject global\.LOOT missing|\[loot-tuning\] (could not read|disabled: missing)|queued loot rules failed
# baseline + loot/tables #18 (2026-11-20, botania:lexicon removed from both Botania inject tables): +1 rule, +2 tables,
# +2 entries removed, +2 pools reweighted, the rest unchanged (judge-7, r1120nv, 2026-11-21)
shell a=$(grep -o '\[loot-tuning\] [0-9]* rules -> rewrote .*' logs/kubejs/server.log | tail -1); b=$(grep -o '\[loot-tuning\] [0-9]* rules -> rewrote .*' "$INST/kubejs/exported/baseline_loot_split_2026-11-17/server_2026-11-16.log" | tail -1 | sed 's/5 rules -> rewrote 184 tables (40 entries removed, 109 pools/6 rules -> rewrote 186 tables (42 entries removed, 111 pools/'); echo "now:  $a"; echo "want: $b"; [ "$a" = "$b" ]
## SQ-LOOT-02 | GlmMerge: one line per reload, nothing lost
@group A
@commands Same boot: grep latest.log for `[GlmMerge]`; `/reload`; grep again
@pass One `[GlmMerge] N entries (lists: ..., fragments: ...)` line after boot and one more after the reload, same N; N = Forge read + added; no `could not read` line. Since P3c (2026-11-17) the members ship fragments only: `fragments: 9 files, 56 entries` and `added` about 50 or more (SQ-RFX-16)
@fails No line: mixin not applied (SQ-LOOT-01). `added` above 0: a `replace: true` list dropped entries before the merge, the `[GlmMerge] skipped` and list lines name them (section 5: a "Fixed" changelog bullet if those modifiers now load and did not before)
bootexpect \[GlmMerge\] \d+ entries \(lists: \d+ files, \d+ entries; fragments: \d+ files
bootreject \[GlmMerge\] could not read
shell grep -hE '\[GlmMerge\]' logs/latest.log | tail -5
> reload
waitlog \[GlmMerge\] \d+ entries 180
reject \[GlmMerge\] could not read
look the N of both lines is the same; `added` and the skipped list (if any) recorded in the run doc
## SQ-LOOT-03 | /dumpall loot dump diff against the pre-split dump is empty
@group A
@commands `/dumpall`; diff `kubejs/exported/loot_tables/` and `loot_runtime_additions.json` against the baseline folder
@pass Both diffs empty, except the two tables added 2026-11-18 under `creativeloot/corpse/` (cave, ocean: "Only in" lines, plan_corpses.md)
@fails A table differs: compare its file; a mod update since 2026-11-15 also shows here (check `mods/` dates before blaming the split)
> dumpall
waitlog \[dumpall\] (all \d+ dumps done|\d+/\d+ (dumps )?ok) 900
shell diff -rq "$INST/kubejs/exported/baseline_loot_split_2026-11-17/loot_tables" kubejs/exported/loot_tables | grep -v "corpse" ; echo LOOT_TABLES_CHECKED
shell diff -q "$INST/kubejs/exported/baseline_loot_split_2026-11-17/loot_runtime_additions.json" kubejs/exported/loot_runtime_additions.json && echo ADDITIONS_SAME
## SQ-LOOT-04 | structure chest tables roll as before: no banned item, tuning active
@group A
@commands `/loottuning`; `/loot spawn` a village house and a dungeon table 10 times each at a cleared spot, then `/cdevtest items` there
@pass `Loot tuning: active`; items rolled; no PneumaticCraft item and no Lightman's Currency coin (both banned); crates (`farmersdelight:*_crate`, `quark:*_sack`) may show where loose food was packed
@fails No items: the table id; banned item present: `07_rules.js` bans did not apply (rule count in SQ-LOOT-01)
> loottuning
sleep 2
expect Loot tuning: active
> forceload add 3200 3200 3216 3216
> fill 3200 -60 3200 3210 -50 3210 minecraft:air
repeat 10
> loot spawn 3205 -58 3205 loot minecraft:chests/village/village_plains_house
> loot spawn 3205 -58 3205 loot minecraft:chests/simple_dungeon
end
sleep 2
> cdevtest items 3205 -58 3205 6
waitlog verb=items 30
expect verb=items .*stacks=[1-9]
reject verb=items .*(pneumaticcraft:|lightmanscurrency:coin)
reject (Unknown (item|block|block type|entity)|Incorrect argument for command|Unknown or incomplete command|That position is not loaded|\[cdevtest\] .*(done=0|error=))
look the item list looks like village house and dungeon loot; crate or sack entries in place of some loose potatoes, carrots, berries
## SQ-LOOT-06 | settings and queued rules carried: loot_config.json unchanged, the CD crate rules still run
@group A
@commands Same boot as SQ-LOOT-01: `/loottuning`; read the KubeJS log for the CD crate pairs
@pass `loot_config.json` settings equal the baseline (`enabled`, `slack`, `log_tables`; the file moved unchanged, Worldgen had no `[loot]` toml section to carry); `/loottuning` lists the Veggies, Vintage, Rustic and Miner's rules as before
@fails CD crate pairs missing: the CD `loot.js` in the pack folder still calls `global.CWG.lootRules` (the jar copy is older until the CD rebuild in P3, the pack folder copy wins in dev)
shell python3 -c "import json,sys; a=json.load(open('kubejs/data/creativeloot/kubejs/loot/loot_config.json'))['settings']; print(a)"
> loottuning
sleep 2
expect Loot tuning: active
shell grep -hiE "crate|bag|sack" logs/kubejs/server.log | grep -iE "veggie|vintage|rustic|miner|cave_carrot" | head -15
look veggie, vintage, rustic and cave carrot crate pairs listed, as SQ-CWG-04 found before the split

