## SQ-LOOT-07 | an ancient corpse: skeleton, unrolled loot, not empty
@group A
@commands `forceload add 0 0`; `summon corpse:corpse 3 -60 3 {Tags:["l07"],Death:{PlayerName:"",ArmorInventory:[{Slot:0,id:"minecraft:leather_boots",Count:1b}]},"creativecompat:corpse":{Ancient:1b,Stage:1b},ForgeData:{"creativeloot:corpse_loot":"creativeloot:corpse/cave"}}`; wait 40 s; read its `creativecompat:corpse`; `loot spawn 3 -58 3 loot creativeloot:corpse/cave`
@pass `Stage: 1b`, `Ancient: 1b`, `EmptiedAt: -1L` after 40 s (it holds the boots); the cave table spawns torches (and sometimes bread)
@fails `EmptiedAt` set: Compat counts the armor slots as empty; the loot command fails: the tables are not in the jar
@absent creativecompat:corpse creativeloot:corpse_loot (NBT keys, not registry ids)
@reviewed 2026-11-20
> forceload add 0 0
> summon corpse:corpse 3 -60 3 {Tags:["l07"],Death:{PlayerName:"",ArmorInventory:[{Slot:0,id:"minecraft:leather_boots",Count:1b}]},"creativecompat:corpse":{Ancient:1b,Stage:1b},ForgeData:{"creativeloot:corpse_loot":"creativeloot:corpse/cave"}}
sleep 40
> data get entity @e[tag=l07,limit=1] "creativecompat:corpse"
expect Stage: 1b
expect EmptiedAt: -1L
> loot spawn 3 -58 3 loot creativeloot:corpse/cave
expect Dropped

## SQ-LOOT-08 | worldgen survey: ancient corpses in a fresh world
@group world
@commands Fresh world (seed of the run); `chunky radius 512` then `chunky start` (64x64 chunks around 0 0); after it finishes, stop the server and count `corpse:corpse` entities in `world/entities/*.mca` with their y and biome (an offline region scan); grep `logs/latest.log` for `creativeloot`
@pass about 4096 / 32 x (share of chunks with a cave floor spot) cave corpses, all at y48 or below, most below y16; ocean ones only on ocean floors, more in cold and deep oceans; no error line from `AncientCorpseFeature`; worldgen time not visibly slower than a run without the jar
@fails none: the biome modifier did not apply (Corpse not loaded, or `ancient_corpses.enabled` false); far fewer than expected: the 3x3 check too strict for deepslate caves (raise `attempts` or `search`)
@phase worldgen
@draft needs an offline entity region scan step (no tool reads entities/*.mca yet)

## SQ-LOOT-09 | Visceral Heap remains never decay or despawn
@group A
@commands `execute in minecraft:the_nether run forceload add 0 0`; `execute in minecraft:the_nether run summon corpse:corpse 0 64 0 {Tags:["l09"],NoGravity:1b,Death:{PlayerName:""},"creativecompat:corpse":{Remains:1b,Stage:1b},ForgeData:{"creativeloot:corpse_remains":1b}}`; wait 6 min; read it
@pass still there after 6 min with `Stage: 1b` (not withered, not removed)
@fails removed after 5 min: Compat applies the empty rules to remains; Stage 2b: the Nether wither rule reached remains
@absent creativecompat:corpse creativeloot:corpse_remains (NBT keys, not registry ids)
@reviewed 2026-11-20
> execute in minecraft:the_nether run forceload add 0 0
> execute in minecraft:the_nether run summon corpse:corpse 0 64 0 {Tags:["l09"],NoGravity:1b,Death:{PlayerName:""},"creativecompat:corpse":{Remains:1b,Stage:1b},ForgeData:{"creativeloot:corpse_remains":1b}}
sleep 360
> execute in minecraft:the_nether run data get entity @e[tag=l09,limit=1] "creativecompat:corpse".Stage
expect 1b
@phase long

## SQ-LOOT-11 | ancient corpse held items and the no-empty guarantee
@group world
@commands In the SQ-LOOT-08 world (same scan): for every `corpse:corpse` with `creativecompat:corpse.Ancient`, read `Death.ArmorInventory`, `Death.MainInventory`, `Death.OffHandInventory`, `NoGravity`
@pass every ancient corpse holds at least one item; about 45% hold a main hand sword or pickaxe (wood, stone, copper, iron) plus about 19% more from the guarantee; about 20% an offhand item, half of them torches (cave) or bread (ocean), 1 to 6 torches, 1 to 3 bread; copper tools carry `state` and `waxed` (unwaxed ones `oxidized`); no ocean corpse has `NoGravity`
@fails a corpse with all three lists empty: `guarantee_tool` off or the hands block not read; ocean corpses with `NoGravity`: an old Loot jar
@absent creativecompat:corpse (an NBT compound key on the corpse entity, not a registry id)
@phase worldgen
@draft needs the offline entity region scan step of SQ-LOOT-08

## CQ-LOOT-12 | ancient corpse held items on the model
@group client
@commands Creative client in the SQ-LOOT-08 world (or a fresh area underground): find ancient corpses holding a tool; open one, take the main hand tool, close; take the offhand item from another
@pass LOOK: the skeleton holds the tool in its right hand and the offhand item (torch, bread or tool) in its left; a copper tool shows its oxidized or waxed texture; once taken out, the item is no longer held within a second
@fails nothing held: the `Equipment` snapshot not written or Compat's `followContents` off; still held after taking it: the main hand snapshot is not matched against the main inventory
@draft no batch holds this row yet; needs a client

## CQ-LOOT-10 | ancient corpse look, first open, remains break
@group client
@commands Creative client near the SQ-LOOT-07 corpse (or `locate`-free: summon one as there with leather and copper armor): look at it, hover with WTHIT, open it, take everything, wait 5 min. In the Nether summon the SQ-LOOT-09 remains and hit them
@pass LOOK: a skeleton wearing the boots; name "Ancient Corpse" on the nameplate and WTHIT; the first open shows torches (the placeholder cave table), a second open by another player shows the same items, not a new roll; emptied, it is gone 5 min later. The remains show "Ancient Remains", break on one hit with a bone sound and drop 1 to 3 bones, sometimes bone chunks, cracked bones and a skeleton skull
@fails "Corpse" name: the lang key is missing from the Loot jar; empty on first open: `CorpseHooks` not registered (Corpse mod id check)
@draft no batch holds this row yet; needs a client

